import Polyfold
/-! Blind formalization of V2_15 (the text's §2.2, Lemma 2.15, p. 25).

Text: the inclusion `i : X_{m+1} → X_m` is continuous for every `m ≥ 0`.

Choices:
- Setting: `X : Type` (spaces put in `Type`; the project's `MPolyfold` is universe-polymorphic,
  this is the instance `u = 0`) with `[TopologicalSpace X] [T2Space X] [ParacompactSpace X]` and
  an M-polyfold structure `P : MPolyfold X` (Definition 2.13; see my
  `RoundTrip/Blind/V2_13.lean`).
- `X_m` with its topology (the paragraph after Definition 2.14) is the project's `P.levelSet m`
  with `P.levelTopology m` (checked with `#print`: the points `x` with `φ(x) ∈ E_m` for a chart
  `φ` of the maximal atlas around `x`, and the topology generated by the sets
  `{x ∈ V | lift of φ(x) to E_m ∈ W}`, `W` open in `E_m`, over those charts — the text's sets
  `φ⁻¹(W)`, `W` open in `O_m`; my `RoundTrip/Blind/V2_14.lean` states that these are the text's
  `X_m` and topology).  The topologies are passed explicitly (the subtype also carries the
  subspace topology of `X`, which is NOT the one meant).
- `i` is the project's `P.levelIncl m` (checked with `#print`: `x ↦ ⟨x, _⟩`, the identity on
  points).
- Nothing looks false to me.
-/
namespace RoundTrip.V2_15
open Polyfold

/-- Lemma 2.15: every inclusion `X_{m+1} → X_m` is continuous. -/
def B : Prop :=
  ∀ (X : Type) [TopologicalSpace X] [T2Space X] [ParacompactSpace X] (P : MPolyfold X) (m : ℕ),
    @Continuous _ _ (P.levelTopology (m + 1)) (P.levelTopology m) (P.levelIncl m)

end RoundTrip.V2_15
